# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, PNOF7 (two coupling subspaces), FULL_OPTIMIZATION.
# FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE: after the occupation-number optimization at the HF orbitals,
# the ADAM / exact-integral-rotation machinery (and, for X2C, the Kramers-restriction
# machinery) is validated on this system and, only if every check passes, ADAM orbital
# rotations (fixed occupations) and occupation re-optimization (fixed orbitals) are
# macro-iterated to convergence (Full_opt/FullOptimization.h).
# NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE and X2C TRUE together: the same molecule is run twice in one
# execution, first NON_REL (real spin-orbitals, plain ADAM), then X2C (complex spinors,
# Kramers-restricted ADAM), so the two FULL_OPTIMIZATION paths can be compared.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL PNOF7
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
